===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|deer|s|pl3qual=nonstandard}}
{{wikipedia}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A ruminant mammal with [[antler]]s and [[hoof|hooves]] of the family {{taxfmt|Cervidae|family}}, or one of several similar animals from related families of the order {{taxfmt|Artiodactyla|order}}.
# {{lb|en|countable|;|in particular}} One of the smaller animals of this family, distinguished from a [[moose]] or [[elk]].
#: {{ux|en|I wrecked my car after a '''deer''' ran across the road.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author={{w|Rumaan Alam}}|title=[[w:Leave the World Behind (novel)|Leave the World Behind]]|publisher=Bloomsbury (2023)|page=76|passage=In the space beyond that, Rose saw a '''deer''', with abbreviated velvet antlers and a cautious yet somehow also bored mien, considering her through dark, strangely human eyes.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[meat]] of such an animal; [[venison]].
#: {{ux|en|Oh, I've never had '''deer''' before.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|;|obsolete|except in the phrase "small deer"}} Any [[animal]], especially a [[quadrupedal]] [[mammal]] as opposed to a bird, fish, etc.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1606|author=William Shakespeare|title=King Lear|section=act III, scene IV
|passage=But mice and rats and such small '''deer''', have been Tom's food for seven long year.}}

